#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268879 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129190 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83af4c85-31c8-5333-8b0c-d044a02bd3da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{x+1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267303} {:answer/id #uuid "8835a210-9de5-5c5f-a9a0-4264ee64fa8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{x+1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267345} {:answer/id #uuid "bda7f1f6-caae-5b5a-912d-ad3b965431f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{x+1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267847} {:answer/id #uuid "c79e2d71-f72b-5349-9f02-4326a7a438da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267934} {:answer/id #uuid "cb9ca14f-93c5-5b93-88bb-be41c8973bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c79e2d71-f72b-5349-9f02-4326a7a438da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267934} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfe90643-e048-5d75-985f-e9ed17b022bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "88491dc6-a6a9-5e2a-ab57-c63ec8866fd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-132574" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}-1}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/92/926e4c717707d13fdb9562e149d2f41c3ab657b42fbae35c0953019ab93a06b6.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-{y}^{2}-1\\le x\\le -y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type I regions.\n\n![](images/89/8933233e8aca4a36ee90ffec69ca6e93d0523d3fa50c400d2cdea78f9ec80812.png)\n\nNotice that the bottom and top boundaries of the left region, written in the form $y=y(x),$  are \n\n$\\,$ $y=\\sqrt{-x-1}\\,$ and $\\,y=1.$\n\nAlso, the bottom and top boundaries of the right region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $y=0\\,$ and $\\,y=-x.$ \n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le -1,\\,\\sqrt{-x-1}\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,0\\le y\\le -x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}-1}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129189 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1723a1-c676-517c-8dc5-f2b61ba017c6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral by Swapping the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa1860a2-38de-5738-988c-ea8e2bfd7c0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}(1 + e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127394} {:answer/id #uuid "0da59dfd-a608-5725-a84d-e1fea7b097f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(1 + e^{-4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127395} {:answer/id #uuid "38c97000-d957-5606-8e43-c28b1ea23edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(1 - e^{-4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127396} {:answer/id #uuid "4c04fbfc-b24a-57f6-9aeb-0d867ff98df2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127397} {:answer/id #uuid "7628f4cd-3ab1-5537-bdcd-2cc5d008f5b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - e^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127398}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3ae90e2c-9b42-50f3-a4dd-8cea89d355b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127393}] :question/id #uuid "c1b66dc5-759e-5b16-9d35-fc67c34a4499" :question/math-academy-id "q-38466" :question/problem "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2}\\displaystyle \\int_{y}^{2}e^{-x^{2}}dxdy$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351412 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129189 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1723a1-c676-517c-8dc5-f2b61ba017c6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral by Swapping the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32fbf319-3234-58a8-95fb-c53b859ed56b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{16}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348902} {:answer/id #uuid "49820777-b895-52a8-9251-7d27144fa1b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}(1-{e}^{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349114} {:answer/id #uuid "6d6fed8a-5620-59e2-bea5-d6cea14b66c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349455} {:answer/id #uuid "6fe1cda9-fe65-5b36-99c7-49ccecf2e000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{16}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349473} {:answer/id #uuid "f9126db6-0a47-59b1-b887-454248d2f098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fe1cda9-fe65-5b36-99c7-49ccecf2e000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{16}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349473} :answer-field/id #uuid "a55be9a3-3b8c-5e73-9f00-cfe58e1d5da1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0524dddc-0711-51cc-bea5-211d12fb3f76" :question/math-academy-id "q-82296" :question/problem "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{8}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/d5/d5d777577f85cd577ce35bfd3a99c1e2218622d1856f4fe7ee4afe1cfd2c9f86.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 8,\\,\\sqrt[3]{y}\\le x\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt[3]{y}\\,⟹\\,y={x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. Its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/05/05ec37a8f4fd33c05a2438df5c5fbc697f8b560fde0b9fe73922a0db56a09c2c.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}[{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}[y]_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{{x}^{4}}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{16}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
